Subject: [PATCH] bd-cbf959: document the iOS/Android app error-report contract
 (platform-tagged /api/v1/logs/error)

Backend keystone for letting companion-app runtime errors flow into Cacophony as
first-class platform errors. Verify-before-implement: the endpoint already
exists (POST /api/v1/logs/error -> handle_log_error), so this is the documented
contract the iOS/Android client beads target, NOT a new endpoint.

Verified:
- Auth: CallerIdentity::Node -> ScopeCheck::Allowed (lib.rs:11707), so the app's
  existing node/operator token can POST /api/v1/logs/error with no new scope grant.
- Empirical acceptance: 'caco log error --component ios-app --labels platform:ios,...'
  surfaces tagged in 'caco log exceptions --component ios-app' (exc-019ef706...).
- Platform filtering already works via the existing --component filter.

Documents the stable platform-tagging convention (component ios-app/android-app,
labels platform:/surface:/kind:, fingerprint dedup guidance, --component
filtering, a verified example) in docs/logs.md + the styled docs/logs.html
sibling (marker resynced; docs/validate-pages.sh passes). Docs-only.
