+## iOS/Android app error reports (platform-tagged)
+
+Companion-app runtime errors — failed button actions, failed daemon requests, response
+decode failures — flow into Cacophony as first-class platform errors through the same
+structured-error ingest endpoint the CLI uses, so iOS/Android surface devs can analyse
+them in the Errors surfaces (`caco log exceptions`, the TUI/Web Errors tab).
+
+**Endpoint.** `POST /api/v1/logs/error` — the same path `caco log error` uses, with
+fields `component`, `summary`, `detail`, `severity`, `fingerprint`, `labels`. The
+endpoint already exists (`handle_log_error`); clients do not need a new route.
+
+**Auth.** The companion apps authenticate with their existing node/operator token. A
+node-identity caller is authorized for every endpoint (`CallerIdentity::Node` resolves to
+an allowed scope check), so the app's token can `POST /api/v1/logs/error` without a new
+scope grant; worker-scope tokens are not used by the apps.
+
+**Platform-tagging convention** (stable — the iOS/Android client beads target this):
+
+| Field | iOS | Android |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `component` | `ios-app` | `android-app` |
+| label `platform:` | `platform:ios` | `platform:android` |
+
+Recommended additional labels:
+
+- `surface:<view>` — the originating screen, e.g. `surface:ContentView`,
+  `surface:AgentDetail`.
+- `kind:<class>` — the failure class: `kind:button` (a failed UI action), `kind:request`
+  (a failed daemon request), `kind:decode` (a response-decode failure).
+
+**Fingerprint guidance (dedup).** Set `fingerprint` to a stable signature of the
+recurring failure, e.g. `<component>:<surface>:<kind>:<stable-error-key>`, omitting
+volatile detail (timestamps, request ids), so a repeatedly-failing button aggregates into
+one Errors row with an occurrence count instead of flooding the surface. When
+`fingerprint` is omitted the daemon derives one from the component and summary.
+
+**Filtering.** Narrow the Errors surface to one platform with the existing component
+filter — `caco log exceptions --component ios-app` / `--component android-app` — plus the
+`platform:` / `surface:` / `kind:` labels for finer analysis.
+
+**Example** (verified end to end):
+
+```bash
+caco log error --project cacophony \
+  --component ios-app \
+  --summary "Save button failed" \
+  --detail "ContentView save -> POST /api/v1/agents/<id>/nudge returned 500" \
+  --severity error \
+  --labels "platform:ios,surface:ContentView,kind:button"
+# surfaces in: caco log exceptions --component ios-app
+```
